% responder_domain — the FAST road domain (road-world s-e812715d step 2; framework L3): the proper response. It beats at
% the world's step (0.1 s) and holds the controls by priority over the planner (priority(responder, planner): "the
% proper response overrides the plan", as the beast case's act over nav). It reads the situation layer's verdicts,
% never a number (rule 2: geometry in the host): when the fold of the ego's pairs asks a longitudinal response
% (resp_lon brake_min_correct | brake_min: RSS Def 10, the rear one brakes) it takes the controls and brakes at that
% response every tick it holds them; when a lateral response stands toward the side a lane change moves to, it stops
% the lateral move; when nothing is asked it gives the controls back (release, done). The host's restrictor (L4)
% caps every command by the same response, so the response holds from the first tick even before the grant
% (ρ = 2 ticks: the want at t, the preempt at t + 1, the latched grant at t + 2).
% Free space (wc-world s-db2f8e59 step 2c; the wheelchair DESIGN v5 §12 position 2): an UNSTRUCTURED pair (a person
% near the chair on a sidewalk, RSS §3.8, ad-rss-lib's) asks resp_unst: brake is the fold's resp_lon(brake_min) as any
% brake (the rules above), continue asks nothing of the ego, drive_away takes the controls and drives toward the
% folded sector, away from every person too close, until the free space asks nothing again. A road never says
% resp_unst (its pairs are lanes'): these rules stay idle there.
% The situation layer's facts are read in full (the keep-table's lead gap machine is safe_long / dangerous now).
catalog responder_domain 1.
provenance text "the road's proper response: brake at the asked response, stop a lateral move, hand the controls back" "2026-10-26".
layers (dyn).
stages (act).
types (obj side constel resp before xcase unst sector).   % completed by the instance (capacity.llp)
include "iface/protocol_domain.llp".
namespace responder produce (dyn).
% the situation layer (semantic_world.situation facts(detail=True), per bound role, and the fold)
pred type(obj, constel) : responder.
pred safe_long(obj) : responder.
pred safe_lat(obj) : responder.
pred dangerous(obj) : responder.
pred safe_before(obj, before) : responder.
pred resp(obj, resp) : responder.
pred safe_lat_left(obj) : responder.
pred safe_lat_right(obj) : responder.
pred resp_side(obj, side, resp) : responder.
pred xing_case(obj, xcase) : responder.
pred xing_before(obj, xcase) : responder.
pred resp_lon(resp) : responder.            % the fold's: the longitudinal response asked of the ego
pred resp_lat(resp) : responder.
pred resp_lat_left(resp) : responder.       % … the lateral one toward each side
pred resp_lat_right(resp) : responder.
pred changing(side) : responder.            % a lane change toward the side runs
pred signalled(obj, side) : responder.      % what a car shows: its indicator (the host's, road-2 item 2), never a belief
pred settled_to(obj, side) : responder.     % ... its lane change seen complete: a pair settled away released from the
                                            %     fold, one settled into my lane decided afresh (the host's situation input)
pred now : responder.                       % the host's beat: one command a tick
pred resp_unst(unst) : responder.           % the free-space fold's response (only where an unstructured pair is)
pred drive_away_sector(sector) : responder. % … the heading it drives away toward (8 sectors: situation.SECTORS)
% the responder's own
pred idle : responder.
pred busy : responder.
pred away : responder.                      % it holds the controls to drive away (free space)
bwd brakes(resp).                           % the responses that brake
brakes(brake_min_correct).
brakes(brake_min).
bwd unst_quiet(unst).                       % the free-space responses that ask nothing of the ego
unst_quiet(none).
unst_quiet(continue).
stage act {
  %% A response is due ({R}): I take the controls.
  guard [dyn] : $resp_lon(R) * $brakes(R) * idle -o busy * tick__active(responder) * tick__want(responder, controls).
  %% My lane change to the left is no longer safe: I take the controls.
  guard_left [dyn] : $changing(left) * $resp_lat_left(R) * $brakes(R) * idle -o busy * tick__active(responder) * tick__want(responder, controls).
  %% My lane change to the right is no longer safe: I take the controls.
  guard_right [dyn] : $changing(right) * $resp_lat_right(R) * $brakes(R) * idle -o busy * tick__active(responder) * tick__want(responder, controls).
  %% People too close and both of us standing: I take the controls to drive away.
  guard_away [dyn] : $resp_unst(drive_away) * idle -o away * tick__active(responder) * tick__want(responder, controls).
  % >>> generated by metis.catalog.protocol_stub: the stop's cancels (regenerate, do not edit)
  %% Stopped: I drop my goal.
  cancel_away [dyn] : tick__cancel(responder) * away -o idle.
  %% Stopped: I drop my goal.
  cancel [dyn] : tick__cancel(responder) * busy -o idle.
  %% Stopped as I finished: nothing left to drop.
  cancel_none [dyn] : idle * tick__cancel(responder) -o idle.   % the race: its done and the stop in one director beat (path_pop, stop_cancel: the sampled order)
  % <<< generated
  %% I brake: the proper response, {R}.
  brake_lon [dyn] : $busy * $tick__grant(responder, controls) * $resp_lon(R) * $brakes(R) * now -o ().
  %% I stop moving left: the lateral response.
  stop_lat_left [dyn] : $busy * $tick__grant(responder, controls) * $changing(left) * $resp_lat_left(R) * $brakes(R) * now -o ().
  %% I stop moving right: the lateral response.
  stop_lat_right [dyn] : $busy * $tick__grant(responder, controls) * $changing(right) * $resp_lat_right(R) * $brakes(R) * now -o ().
  %% I drive away from them, toward {S}.
  drive_away [dyn] : $away * $tick__grant(responder, controls) * $resp_unst(drive_away) * $drive_away_sector(S) * now -o ().
  %% The free space asks nothing of me again: the plan has the controls again.
  away_done [dyn] : away * $resp_unst(R) * $unst_quiet(R) -o idle * tick__done(responder) * tick__release(responder, controls).
  %% Nothing asks a response: the plan has the controls again.
  stand_down [dyn] : busy * $resp_lon(none) * $resp_lat_left(none) * $resp_lat_right(none) -o idle * tick__done(responder) * tick__release(responder, controls).
}
